# What must never enter the backend build context.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs requirements.txt and app/, but the context is still
# uploaded to the daemon in full before any COPY runs. Without this file that
# upload included .venv (hundreds of MB, and Linux-incompatible macOS wheels),
# every uploaded recording, every rendered export and the SQLite database -
# customer audio shipped into an image build, and a build that got slower the
# longer the app had been used.

.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Runtime state. These are bind-mounted at run time (see docker-compose.yml);
# baking a copy in would ship someone's media inside the image.
uploads/
exports/
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite3

# Not needed to run the service.
tests/
requirements-dev.txt

.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
